The Watts On backend is derived from TheRealBatBro/Home-Assistant-Novafos-V2
(Novafos water via Watts On):

  https://github.com/TheRealBatBro/Home-Assistant-Novafos-V2

Derived files (each carries a header saying it is derived and that changes
were made):
  custom_components/kmd_easy_energy/api/wattson_client.py

The Watts On login flow (Azure AD B2C app registration, PKCE + msauth://
redirect, rotating refresh token), the API base URL and the endpoint and
field names for water were learned from that project (upstream commit
920e41f) and reimplemented for district heating; no code was copied
verbatim. Heat endpoints and heat field names are not from the upstream
project (it only covers water) and are unverified guesses.

